From 0d58963e6694233dd05ffc0416d8c1e305a3d7c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zabeelbasheer <53309631+zabeelbasheer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 18:51:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix: force JSON mode + low reasoning effort on structured
 Groq calls; add skip-intake preliminary audit path

gpt-oss-120b is a reasoning model. Groq's own docs and community forum
confirm it sometimes puts content in the reasoning field instead of
content, which broke json.loads() in evaluator.py and vendor_detector.py,
silently defaulting most criteria to the score=1 fallback. Added
response_format={type:json_object} to force clean JSON in content,
and reasoning_effort=low everywhere, both for reliability and latency,
this is simple extraction/scoring, not a task needing deep reasoning.

Also adds a skip_intake option: a secondary button that scores the raw
description directly, no clarifying questions, for a fast preliminary
read before committing to the full intake conversation.
